"Keep in mind that these values are for the example indicated above.  They "
"may vary depending on the system."
msgstr "请注意，这些值适用于上述示例。  根据系统的不同，实际值可能有所变化。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/multimedia/_index.adoc:241
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Resampling Quality"
msgstr "重采样质量"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/multimedia/_index.adoc:244
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The process of changing the sample rate of an audio stream is called "
"resampling."
msgstr "改变音频流采样率的过程称为重采样。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/multimedia/_index.adoc:246
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This usually happens automatically in situations like recording audio with a "
"DI (Digital Interface) or simply when playing back audio files with very low "
"resolution."
msgstr "这种情况通常会自动发生，例如使用 DI（数字接口）录制音频，或者播放分辨率很低的音频文件时。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/multimedia/_index.adoc:248
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Example: DI uses 192000 kHz, application only accepts 48000 kHz (or the "
"other way around)."
msgstr "例如：DI 使用 192000 kHz，而应用程序仅接受 48000 kHz（反之亦然）。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/multimedia/_index.adoc:250
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If possible, this should be adjusted outside the sound device driver, but "
"for cases where this is not possible (Or the hardware is bad at resampling), "
"you have influence over the quality that is used for resampling."
msgstr "如果可能，应在声卡设备驱动程序之外调整采样率；但在无法做到这一点（或硬件重采样效果不佳）的情况下，你可以调整重采样质量。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/multimedia/_index.adoc:252
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Should you be unsure if you need this, for normal music listening, doing "
"meetings and so on the default value is totally fine and most applications "
"use 48000 kHz anyway, so resampling rarely happens."
msgstr "如果不确定是否需要调整，对于日常听音乐、参加会议等用途，默认值完全够用，而且大多数应用程序也使用 48000 kHz，因此很少发生重采样。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/multimedia/_index.adoc:254
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"When making music, recording sounds otherwise where quality matters or you "
"are an audiophile, you can increase the resampling quality."
